From 1a5a0aa1f2b5e0f983c77de6ccc578e0acf55706 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:28:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add r9fs workflow: build the Rust kernel on the runner and
 run the r9fs suite

r9fs needs CONFIG_RUST and an r9fs.ko from the same commit as the
Image, which the published Image line does not provide, and
ghcr.io/v9fs/docker has no Rust toolchain. r9fs.yml (manual, arm64
runner) installs clang, rustc 1.99.0 + rust-src and bindgen-cli 0.73.2
(scripts/v9fs-install-rust-toolchain), builds the Image + r9fs.ko from
linux_repository@linux_ref, and runs v9fs-run-tests r9fs in the harness
container.

v9fs-prepare-r9fs takes R9FS_KO so a caller can stage another module
built from the same kernel commit. v9fs-run-tests keeps r9fs.log in
logs/<ts>/.
---
