 ## Unreleased
 
 - Add `r9fs` suite for the read-only Rust 9P2000.L file system (`fs/r9fs`, v9fs/linux branch `cursor/r9fs-rust-virtio-f6e3`; agent-team D0004). `qemu.bash` adds two virtio-9p devices (`r9share`, and `r9slow` with `throttling.bps-read`) when `R9FS_SHARE` is set. `scripts/v9fs-r9fs-tests` moves them from `9pnet_virtio` to `r9fs_virtio` and diffs an r9fs manifest against the C v9fs view of the same host directory. It also checks read-only/negative cases, kill latency of a stalled reader, and that unbinding the device fails a posted read instead of waiting for it. `scripts/v9fs-kmod` loads modules (the chroot has no kmod). `scripts/v9fs-build-r9fs-kernel` builds the Rust-enabled Image + `r9fs.ko` outside the container (no Rust toolchain in `ghcr.io/v9fs/docker`). Not wired into Actions yet.
+- Add `.github/workflows/r9fs.yml` (manual, `ubuntu-24.04-arm`). It installs clang, rustc 1.99.0 + rust-src and bindgen-cli 0.73.2 (`scripts/v9fs-install-rust-toolchain`), builds the Image + `r9fs.ko` from `linux_repository`@`linux_ref`, and runs `v9fs-run-tests r9fs` in `ghcr.io/v9fs/docker`. `v9fs-prepare-r9fs` takes `R9FS_KO` (a module from the same kernel commit). `v9fs-run-tests` keeps `r9fs.log` in `logs/<ts>/`.
 
 - t0011 allsquash: patch `--squashuser=$(id -un)` in prepare so `exp/` ownership matches the runner; drop t0011 rows from `diod/xfail.txt` (#28 / agent-team#5 / [test#31](https://github.com/v9fs/test/pull/31)).
 
